        "original_id": "bf1ea759-3dde-5adc-b351-dd34a0635482",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Virgilia, Koeleria, Leto venus\n- Taxa and families: Fabaceae, grass family\n- Places: Southern Africa, Antarctica, oceanic islands\n\nFacts:\n- Virgilia is a genus of Southern African trees in the family Fabaceae.\n- Virgilia has shiny to hairy pinnate leaves, mauve to pink pea-shaped flowers, and leathery pods.\n- Koeleria is a common and widespread genus of plants in the grass family.\n- Koeleria is found on all continents except Antarctica and on various oceanic islands.\n- Leto venus uses Virgilia as its larval food plant.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
